WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.479 --> 00:00:01.926
- Good morning believe nation!

00:00:01.926 --> 00:00:03.898
My name is Alex and my one word is belong.

00:00:03.898 --> 00:00:05.105
And I believe that the world

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.240
would be a better place

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.283
if more people felt that they belonged.

00:00:08.283 --> 00:00:09.622
To help you on your journey,

00:00:09.622 --> 00:00:10.559
today's message is,

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:12.492
don't stop!

00:00:12.492 --> 00:00:14.248
Over to you, Tony Robbins.

00:00:14.248 --> 00:00:16.177
(rooster crowing)

00:00:16.177 --> 00:00:19.285
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.242
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:21.242 --> 00:00:24.742
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:26.477 --> 00:00:28.351
- There is another level.

00:00:28.351 --> 00:00:29.883
The only reason you keep seeing

00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:31.989
there isn't is you feel so exhausted about

00:00:31.989 --> 00:00:32.822
where you are.

00:00:32.822 --> 00:00:34.516
But life, the universe or God

00:00:34.516 --> 00:00:36.030
is just testing you

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.594
because there is another level.

00:00:37.594 --> 00:00:38.483
If this is good,

00:00:38.483 --> 00:00:39.960
giant shift to excellence,

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.723
giant, start poor to good to excellence.

00:00:43.723 --> 00:00:47.235
There's a level where all
your dreams are realized.

00:00:47.235 --> 00:00:50.054
There's a level that you've
always dreamed about.

00:00:50.054 --> 00:00:50.887
It is real,

00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:52.436
it has not gone away.

00:00:52.436 --> 00:00:54.426
But it takes that extra burst

00:00:54.426 --> 00:00:56.149
when you think there's nothing left,

00:00:56.149 --> 00:00:57.413
there's no way.

00:00:57.413 --> 00:00:59.500
You've tried everything 10 million times

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:00.419
and you keep going.

00:01:00.419 --> 00:01:02.390
It's almost like God is
saying if you keep hitting

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:03.630
this wall enough times,

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.635
I will see that you will not stop,

00:01:05.635 --> 00:01:07.508
that you are filled with that level

00:01:07.508 --> 00:01:09.474
of determination and faith and courage

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:10.521
and then the door opens.

00:01:10.521 --> 00:01:11.843
And you get to that next level.

00:01:11.843 --> 00:01:14.281
And what most people don't know is

00:01:14.281 --> 00:01:17.299
the next level is just

00:01:17.299 --> 00:01:18.731
two millimeters above

00:01:18.731 --> 00:01:21.230
and it's called outstanding
ladies and gentlemen.

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:22.888
Outstanding!

00:01:22.888 --> 00:01:24.263
What's it called?

00:01:24.263 --> 00:01:25.810
(audience cheering)

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:26.643
What's it called?

00:01:26.643 --> 00:01:27.476
- [Audience] Outstanding

00:01:27.476 --> 00:01:28.309
What's it called?

00:01:28.309 --> 00:01:29.391
- [Audience] Outstanding!

00:01:29.391 --> 00:01:32.144
- Outstanding, magnificent, unstoppable,

00:01:32.144 --> 00:01:35.359
extraordinary, not excellent.

00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:37.665
It's a different level.

00:01:37.665 --> 00:01:40.472
It's a level where you
are not one of the best,

00:01:40.472 --> 00:01:42.107
you are the best.

00:01:42.107 --> 00:01:43.730
And you know what's amazing,

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:45.164
you only have to be two millimeters

00:01:45.164 --> 00:01:47.422
more than everybody else
and you get everything.

00:01:47.422 --> 00:01:48.922
You get the joy, the laughter, the fun,

00:01:48.922 --> 00:01:50.749
the family, the passion, the economics,

00:01:50.749 --> 00:01:53.035
the freedom, the spirit, it's all there.

00:01:53.035 --> 00:01:56.088
What Jerry Maguire called the Quan baby,

00:01:56.088 --> 00:01:58.041
all of it.

00:01:58.041 --> 00:01:59.996
And it's just two millimeters above

00:01:59.996 --> 00:02:02.466
and most excellent people give up

00:02:02.466 --> 00:02:04.096
because they are exhausted.

00:02:04.096 --> 00:02:05.378
And there are some people who go,

00:02:05.378 --> 00:02:06.365
"The harder I hit it,

00:02:06.365 --> 00:02:07.370
the more I hit it,

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.007
sooner or later it's going down.

00:02:09.007 --> 00:02:10.183
I'm not stopping."

00:02:10.183 --> 00:02:11.483
And when you do that enough,

00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:12.988
it pops open.

00:02:12.988 --> 00:02:14.821
- This message resonated for me a lot

00:02:14.821 --> 00:02:15.654
on two levels.

00:02:15.654 --> 00:02:17.402
I actually want to share
a quick story with you.

00:02:17.402 --> 00:02:19.586
Navy Seals have some
of the hardest training

00:02:19.586 --> 00:02:21.257
that they have to go through

00:02:21.257 --> 00:02:24.065
both mental and physical to graduate.

00:02:24.065 --> 00:02:26.072
And one of the most difficult
things that they have

00:02:26.072 --> 00:02:28.340
to go through is called Hell week.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:29.268
In this one week,

00:02:29.268 --> 00:02:30.736
they sleep probably anywhere

00:02:30.736 --> 00:02:33.577
from four to 10 hours in a seven day span.

00:02:33.577 --> 00:02:36.671
Both their mind, their
body and their spirit

00:02:36.671 --> 00:02:39.809
gets pushed to the limits.

00:02:39.809 --> 00:02:41.490
Now here's the thing,

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.949
they'd been training for this hell week

00:02:43.949 --> 00:02:46.402
surviving things like drown proofing

00:02:46.402 --> 00:02:48.630
where their arms and legs get tied.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:49.864
They get tossed in a pool

00:02:49.864 --> 00:02:51.503
and they essentially have to get used

00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:52.681
to being drowned.

00:02:52.681 --> 00:02:55.863
These are top specimens
that you can think of

00:02:55.863 --> 00:02:58.354
both physically and
mentally men and women.

00:02:58.354 --> 00:03:00.242
And in this last week they just

00:03:00.242 --> 00:03:02.939
need to graduate and
survive one more week.

00:03:02.939 --> 00:03:05.433
And so here's the thing
that's mind blowing.

00:03:05.433 --> 00:03:07.140
Every morning whether it's

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.593
three am or four am,

00:03:08.593 --> 00:03:10.185
when their instructor wakes them up,

00:03:10.185 --> 00:03:12.039
they line up on the beach.

00:03:12.039 --> 00:03:13.007
And next to them,

00:03:13.007 --> 00:03:14.351
there's a brass bell.

00:03:14.351 --> 00:03:16.674
If they want to quit all they have to do

00:03:16.674 --> 00:03:17.507
is ring the bell.

00:03:17.507 --> 00:03:18.802
They ring the bell,

00:03:18.802 --> 00:03:20.459
they quit, that's it, it's done.

00:03:20.459 --> 00:03:21.818
They pack up the stuff and leave.

00:03:21.818 --> 00:03:23.360
Do you want to know what's

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.622
the mind blowing thing?

00:03:24.622 --> 00:03:27.716
Most people quit not when they get their

00:03:27.716 --> 00:03:30.251
hands tied and thrown in the pool.

00:03:30.251 --> 00:03:32.464
When they have to jump
into ice cold water.

00:03:32.464 --> 00:03:33.883
When they have to hold

00:03:33.883 --> 00:03:37.467
a log over their head
for four or five hours.

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:38.732
Most people quit

00:03:38.732 --> 00:03:40.081
in the morning.

00:03:40.081 --> 00:03:43.546
Most people quit at the
idea of doing those tasks.

00:03:43.546 --> 00:03:45.324
Only a handful of people

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:48.621
actually quit while they're
struggling through it,

00:03:48.621 --> 00:03:50.660
while they're trying to hold their breath

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.604
and get used to being drowned.

00:03:52.604 --> 00:03:54.240
So what does it tell you

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.508
about the human capacity?

00:03:55.508 --> 00:03:57.481
A lot of the people that ring the bell

00:03:57.481 --> 00:04:00.542
are quitting because of
the idea of what's coming.

00:04:00.542 --> 00:04:02.656
While most people when they actually,

00:04:02.656 --> 00:04:03.758
when they get into it,

00:04:03.758 --> 00:04:05.178
they make it through.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.572
And isn't that the truth?

00:04:06.572 --> 00:04:08.292
Isn't the thing that psyches us out,

00:04:08.292 --> 00:04:09.801
the thing that we hold ourselves

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:12.373
back on is the idea of
going back to the gym?

00:04:12.373 --> 00:04:14.554
Is the idea of doing that last set

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:15.571
if you're working out.

00:04:15.571 --> 00:04:17.128
Is the idea that you want to read

00:04:17.128 --> 00:04:19.299
that extra book to get better at something

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:21.832
that you're trying to learn
about, leadership or whatever.

00:04:21.832 --> 00:04:23.919
So here's the thing

00:04:23.919 --> 00:04:25.012
that you can learn from Navy Seals

00:04:25.012 --> 00:04:27.366
while being in the moment
as something difficult

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:28.253
is coming your way

00:04:28.253 --> 00:04:29.577
and you don't want to stop.

00:04:29.577 --> 00:04:31.739
Remember that it's a state of mind

00:04:31.739 --> 00:04:33.231
that often people quit in,

00:04:33.231 --> 00:04:35.613
not when they're in the situation.

00:04:35.613 --> 00:04:37.257
So anytime you start doubting yourself,

00:04:37.257 --> 00:04:38.322
anytime you want to stop,

00:04:38.322 --> 00:04:39.871
anytime you want to quit on something

00:04:39.871 --> 00:04:41.132
that's important to you,

00:04:41.132 --> 00:04:42.647
realize that my fear,

00:04:42.647 --> 00:04:44.172
the reason I want to stop,

00:04:44.172 --> 00:04:47.473
the reason I want to quit is
simply because I'm imagining

00:04:47.473 --> 00:04:48.880
how difficult it's going to be.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:50.171
But once you put yourself

00:04:50.171 --> 00:04:51.230
in that situation just like

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.063
those Navy Seals,

00:04:52.063 --> 00:04:53.339
you'll make it through.

00:04:53.339 --> 00:04:55.854
And the second thing
that's really important,

00:04:55.854 --> 00:04:57.140
is to raise your standards.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:58.471
It's important, just like

00:04:58.471 --> 00:04:59.629
Tony talks about it,

00:04:59.629 --> 00:05:01.841
for greatness to happen,

00:05:01.841 --> 00:05:04.984
don't be okay when things are just fine.

00:05:04.984 --> 00:05:07.183
Or okay, or they're alright.

00:05:07.183 --> 00:05:08.962
Push through the wall,

00:05:08.962 --> 00:05:10.429
'Cause ultimately,

00:05:10.429 --> 00:05:13.476
that's where greatness waits for you.

00:05:13.476 --> 00:05:14.891
So the question of the day is,

00:05:14.891 --> 00:05:16.268
where in your life right now

00:05:16.268 --> 00:05:17.842
you're seeing some success

00:05:17.842 --> 00:05:19.117
that you don't want to stop in

00:05:19.117 --> 00:05:21.677
and what can you do about it right now?

00:05:21.677 --> 00:05:23.297
Leave your comments
below, I'm really excited

00:05:23.297 --> 00:05:24.391
to see what you have to say.

00:05:24.391 --> 00:05:26.117
I also want to give a big shout out

00:05:26.117 --> 00:05:27.366
to Scott J. Weaver Sr.

00:05:27.366 --> 00:05:29.700
Scott thanks so much for
purchasing your One Word,

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.100
it really means a lot to us

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.625
and I hope you are enjoying the book.

00:05:32.625 --> 00:05:34.110
Thank you so much for watching.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:35.085
We believe in you

00:05:35.085 --> 00:05:36.182
and we hope you continue

00:05:36.182 --> 00:05:37.692
to believe in yourself and

00:05:37.692 --> 00:05:39.788
whatever your one word is.

00:05:39.788 --> 00:05:41.395
And we'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:05:41.395 --> 00:05:43.420
for another shot of Ent spresso.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.603
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:46.603 --> 00:05:50.020
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:05:53.358 --> 00:05:55.816
- I've learned,

00:05:55.816 --> 00:05:59.800
if you're a farmer.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:03.281
A farmer understands

00:06:03.281 --> 00:06:04.442
better than any

00:06:04.442 --> 00:06:06.771
other worker in this country.

00:06:06.771 --> 00:06:08.626
A farmer has an understanding

00:06:08.626 --> 00:06:10.439
that most people

00:06:10.439 --> 00:06:13.647
never achieve in their life.

00:06:13.647 --> 00:06:15.742
I really respect

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:18.702
the farmers and their commitment.

00:06:18.702 --> 00:06:21.828
But I respect also their understanding.

00:06:21.828 --> 00:06:24.828
My Grandfather,

00:06:24.828 --> 00:06:27.942
my Uncle

00:06:27.942 --> 00:06:30.057
the thing was

00:06:30.057 --> 00:06:32.665
to wake up early in the morning,

00:06:32.665 --> 00:06:36.649
before you start your day,

00:06:36.649 --> 00:06:38.802
you start your day

00:06:38.802 --> 00:06:40.786
by feeding all the animals.

00:06:40.786 --> 00:06:43.363
I never understood that.

00:06:43.363 --> 00:06:46.452
Why am I feeding, slopping these hogs,

00:06:46.452 --> 00:06:48.901
bailing this hay for these cows.

00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:51.158
taking the food out to the hunting dogs,

00:06:51.158 --> 00:06:53.759
going to getting these mules and horses,

00:06:53.759 --> 00:06:55.860
walking 'em down to water?

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:58.747
Why am I feeding these chickens man?

00:06:58.747 --> 00:07:01.125
All this before I eat?

00:07:01.125 --> 00:07:02.956
My Grandfather set me down,

00:07:02.956 --> 00:07:04.276
he said, "Young man,

00:07:04.276 --> 00:07:06.897
if we don't take care of these animals,

00:07:06.897 --> 00:07:09.107
that we are requiring

00:07:09.107 --> 00:07:10.479
to take care of us,"

00:07:10.479 --> 00:07:12.777
he said, "What's going to happen to us?"

00:07:12.777 --> 00:07:15.071
He said, "We depended on them chickens

00:07:15.071 --> 00:07:16.905
to lay eggs,

00:07:16.905 --> 00:07:19.155
to give us meat.

00:07:19.155 --> 00:07:20.238
We depended on

00:07:20.238 --> 00:07:21.810
them hogs for meat .

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.424
We depended on them mules

00:07:23.424 --> 00:07:25.835
to pull the plow so we could plant.

00:07:25.835 --> 00:07:27.833
We depended on them horses

00:07:27.833 --> 00:07:30.252
to drag all these wagons around.

00:07:30.252 --> 00:07:32.807
We depended on these hunting dogs

00:07:32.807 --> 00:07:35.474
to go out in the woods and uncover

00:07:35.474 --> 00:07:37.624
the animals for us."

00:07:37.624 --> 00:07:40.376
He said, "And what

00:07:40.376 --> 00:07:42.594
I respect about farmers is,

00:07:42.594 --> 00:07:44.737
they understand that everything

00:07:44.737 --> 00:07:47.012
comes in seasons.

00:07:47.012 --> 00:07:49.378
There is a planting season

00:07:49.378 --> 00:07:52.182
and you got to plant and plant and plant

00:07:52.182 --> 00:07:55.189
and plant, plow, till, hoe the rows.

00:07:55.189 --> 00:07:57.087
You got to do all that.

00:07:57.087 --> 00:08:01.196
Seed it, fertilize it

00:08:01.196 --> 00:08:03.939
in order for a crop to grow.

00:08:03.939 --> 00:08:08.095
Now here's what happens some years,

00:08:08.095 --> 00:08:10.708
some years there's a drought.

00:08:10.708 --> 00:08:13.571
Ain't no rain, ain't no crops.

00:08:13.571 --> 00:08:15.646
Some times it's a flood.

00:08:15.646 --> 00:08:17.341
Wipe out all the crops,

00:08:17.341 --> 00:08:21.122
all the plants, but guess what,

00:08:21.122 --> 00:08:23.609
you still got to do the plant.

00:08:23.609 --> 00:08:25.951
Because what you're banking on

00:08:25.951 --> 00:08:27.515
is just enough rain,

00:08:27.515 --> 00:08:29.695
just enough sunshine

00:08:29.695 --> 00:08:32.504
so you can harvest.

00:08:32.504 --> 00:08:35.164
And even if they crops get washed out,

00:08:35.164 --> 00:08:37.270
even if the floods come,

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:39.139
even of the drought come,

00:08:39.139 --> 00:08:43.126
the thing about the farmer,
they do it all again.

00:08:43.126 --> 00:08:44.909
Because they understand

00:08:44.909 --> 00:08:48.100
that eventually you'll
be able to harvest."

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:50.315
And that's what I respect about farmers

00:08:50.315 --> 00:08:52.409
and that's my life.

00:08:52.409 --> 00:08:54.838
- I wanted to talk to you about like

00:08:54.838 --> 00:08:56.409
is it, the transition that

00:08:56.409 --> 00:08:58.160
very successful people make

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.884
and either they make it or they don't.

00:08:59.884 --> 00:09:02.429
And the transition is
to go from being hungry

00:09:02.429 --> 00:09:03.940
and filled with all this angst

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:06.966
to being like stupid, wealthy and famous

00:09:06.966 --> 00:09:09.645
but still keeping your art relevant.

00:09:09.645 --> 00:09:11.119
How do you do that?

00:09:11.119 --> 00:09:13.730
- Ah huh, we're still

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:15.591
super competitive people.

00:09:15.591 --> 00:09:18.692
We're really perfectionists and we hate

00:09:18.692 --> 00:09:20.187
to let each other down.

00:09:20.187 --> 00:09:23.097
There's always a better riff coming.

00:09:23.097 --> 00:09:26.434
There's always a better album.

00:09:26.434 --> 00:09:28.889
Maybe there's the never satisfied part

00:09:28.889 --> 00:09:32.173
to us that will keep us going till we die.

00:09:32.173 --> 00:09:34.066
There's always the ultimate lyric

00:09:34.066 --> 00:09:35.678
that's going to connect

00:09:35.678 --> 00:09:37.333
to everyone in the world or something.

00:09:37.333 --> 00:09:40.611
There is always a better something

00:09:40.611 --> 00:09:42.077
that we haven't got yet.

00:09:42.077 --> 00:09:44.155
- Like the man said you pick up the pace.

00:09:44.155 --> 00:09:46.163
If you don't pick up the pace,

00:09:46.163 --> 00:09:47.608
you'll be left behind.

00:09:47.608 --> 00:09:49.584
I'm amazed at the people

00:09:49.584 --> 00:09:53.313
that lack the flexibility
to pick up the pace.

00:09:53.313 --> 00:09:55.525
They just get in a rut.

00:09:55.525 --> 00:09:57.596
I stroll down here,

00:09:57.596 --> 00:09:59.538
and I'm going to stroll back.

00:09:59.538 --> 00:10:02.582
I'm going to stroll over here,

00:10:02.582 --> 00:10:03.666
I'm going to stroll over there.

00:10:03.666 --> 00:10:04.656
One of the most

00:10:04.656 --> 00:10:07.826
amazing things about
the disaster at Malaysia

00:10:07.826 --> 00:10:08.872
is when it happened,

00:10:08.872 --> 00:10:11.140
everybody had to pick up the pace.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:13.273
All the news media had
to pick up the pace.

00:10:13.273 --> 00:10:15.144
They were booking night flights

00:10:15.144 --> 00:10:16.130
and they were flying over here

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:17.053
and flying over there.

00:10:17.053 --> 00:10:18.603
Somebody had to work overtime.

00:10:18.603 --> 00:10:20.481
Won't be home for three days.

00:10:20.481 --> 00:10:22.070
Typing in the middle of the night,

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:23.395
research going on

00:10:23.395 --> 00:10:25.080
because when something happens,

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:26.813
everybody got to pick up the pace.

00:10:26.813 --> 00:10:29.385
That's why I can't deal with people

00:10:29.385 --> 00:10:32.288
who cannot pick up the pace.

00:10:32.288 --> 00:10:34.837
Don't be strolling

00:10:34.837 --> 00:10:36.664
when I got to a 911 on you.

00:10:36.664 --> 00:10:38.209
I need people who can

00:10:38.209 --> 00:10:40.036
pick up the pace.

00:10:40.036 --> 00:10:43.003
(congregation cheering)

00:10:43.003 --> 00:10:46.240
It's like the neighbor
said, "Pick up the pace!"

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:48.349
Something is about to happen,

00:10:48.349 --> 00:10:49.491
pick up the pace.

00:10:49.491 --> 00:10:50.945
Something's about to happen,

00:10:50.945 --> 00:10:51.961
pick up the pace.

00:10:51.961 --> 00:10:53.203
Something is about to happen,

00:10:53.203 --> 00:10:54.036
pick up the pace.

00:10:54.036 --> 00:10:55.119
Something is about to happen,

00:10:55.119 --> 00:10:56.035
pick up the pace.

00:10:56.035 --> 00:10:57.346
Something is about to happen,

00:10:57.346 --> 00:10:58.321
pick up the pace.

00:10:58.321 --> 00:11:00.078
Something is about to happen,

00:11:00.078 --> 00:11:01.536
I came to tell the young people.

00:11:01.536 --> 00:11:04.517
Pick up the pace, pick up
the pace, pick up the pace.

00:11:04.517 --> 00:11:07.272
Something is about to happen!

00:11:07.272 --> 00:11:09.554
The danger of low expectations.

00:11:09.554 --> 00:11:12.828
(congregation cheering)

00:11:12.828 --> 00:11:14.188
I would rather aim

00:11:14.188 --> 00:11:15.348
for the satrs,

00:11:15.348 --> 00:11:16.640
and not hit them

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:19.613
than to not aim at all.

00:11:19.613 --> 00:11:22.412
I would rather go after it and not get it

00:11:22.412 --> 00:11:24.442
than not go after it at all.

00:11:24.442 --> 00:11:26.303
I'd rather try and fail

00:11:26.303 --> 00:11:27.867
than not try at all.

00:11:27.867 --> 00:11:30.590
I don't want to live with the idea,

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:33.179
I wonder what would have happened

00:11:33.179 --> 00:11:34.902
had I done more with my life.

00:11:34.902 --> 00:11:37.315
I'm going to go for it

00:11:37.315 --> 00:11:39.790
come Hell of high water.

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:42.954
I'm going after my destiny.

00:11:42.954 --> 00:11:44.970
Touch your neighbor and say run!

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.253
- [Congregation] Run!

00:11:46.253 --> 00:11:48.734
You got to run after your destiny.

00:11:48.734 --> 00:11:51.559
You can't stroll after your destiny.

00:11:51.559 --> 00:11:54.200
You can't walk after your destiny.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:56.528
You got to run!

00:11:56.528 --> 00:11:58.133
Somebody holler run!

00:11:58.133 --> 00:12:02.050
- [Congregation] Run!

00:12:04.924 --> 00:12:06.687
- You got to run.

00:12:06.687 --> 00:12:08.323
You got to run.

00:12:08.323 --> 00:12:09.573
You got to run.

00:12:09.573 --> 00:12:11.893
You can't just wake up

00:12:11.893 --> 00:12:14.447
in the morning and let me see
what's going to happen today.

00:12:14.447 --> 00:12:15.838
I don't know what I'm going to do.

00:12:15.838 --> 00:12:17.164
I don't know what I'm going to wear.

00:12:17.164 --> 00:12:18.437
I don't know what I'm going to cook.

00:12:18.437 --> 00:12:19.993
I don't know where I'm going to go.

00:12:19.993 --> 00:12:21.310
I just woke up.

00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:23.735
Ah, you should just stay in the bed.

00:12:23.735 --> 00:12:25.459
Give the day to somebody

00:12:25.459 --> 00:12:27.525
whose going to run after their destiny.

00:12:27.525 --> 00:12:30.715
Give the day to somebody who has a plan,

00:12:30.715 --> 00:12:33.079
who has a strategy

00:12:33.079 --> 00:12:35.727
because success is never an accident

00:12:35.727 --> 00:12:37.103
and if you don't want it,

00:12:37.103 --> 00:12:38.513
get out of my way.

00:12:38.513 --> 00:12:40.326
Because there are some people

00:12:40.326 --> 00:12:43.562
who want to do something with their life,

00:12:43.562 --> 00:12:44.979
who will run.

